cription  pretty graphics pixels and triangles  aren't the only things to get excited  about  sound is also taking a big leap around  you  with 3d audio but there's a few key  differences to keep in mind between both  the ps5 and the xbox series x  let's start with playstation the ps5 is  all about its tempest  3d audio tech however for the ps5 3d  audio will not be supported through  tv speakers and surround sound systems  at launch  making headphone audio as playstation  architect mark cerny put it  the current gold standard for 3d audio  it is coming eventually though  for headphones there is the pulse 3d  wireless headset which has been  engineered  to fully show off the ps5's audio  capabilities  some developers are specifically  designing their sound to make the most  of the console's new audio opportunities  such as capcom for resident evil village  thankfully you don't need the pulse  headset to get that rich immersive sound  experience  a broad range of headphones will work  and you'll need to plug them in the ps5  via usb  or into the dual sensor's 3.5 millimeter  audio jack  sony is working to eventually bring its  3d audio to tv speakers and surround  sound system so when that day comes  we suggest taking a look at dolby atmos  supported sound bars  xbox series x already supports dolby  atmos tech  so that way you can't go wrong with  either console especially if you get  both  that said the xbox series x also  features native 3d sound support with  dts x and as just mentioned  dolby atmos in fact at this very moment  dts x is actually supported with the  xbox one with games like gears 5  resident evil 2 final fantasy xv and a  bunch of others taking full advantage of  it  so to wrap it up just make sure that  whatever sound bar you're getting it  supports dolby atmos  ones like the sennheiser mbo or the sony  ht  st5000 in the case that having a  surround system or sound bar isn't a big  concern to you  the lg cx tv mentioned earlier has dolby  atmos su